invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: srv_ext_duplicate compares only the types this build recognizes, so a
  block carrying two extensions of one unknown type passes, and RFC 9846
  §4.3 forbids more than one extension of any type in a block
  (rfc9846.txt:1673-1674). srv_parser.h states that the predicate
  answers for every type, which is why it walks the block rather than
  reading the seen mask. test/srv_parser_tests.h appends a second GREASE
  extension and requires illegal_parameter.

--- old
        if (type_before(exts, before, type)) {
--- new
        if (srv_ext_known(type) && type_before(exts, before, type)) {
